    "Notes Updated": "8/30/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter?\n Cross body, low arm slot delivery, though Statcast doesn't have it as that low of a slot (I don't buy it)\n Interesting arm angle seems to really help the fastballs play\n Slider is probably more cutter than slider, hovers around an average offering\n Changeup looks like an above average pitch, potentially better\n Added a curve that I think is fringe average currently, but I like what it does for the overall repertoire, giving another velo band to worry about\n Command is still very fringy, and could lead to a future in the bullpen, but I think he can be a solid lefty out of the pen if that ends up the case.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/25/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Starter?\n Cross body, low arm slot delivery\n Interesting arm angle seems to really help the fastball play\n Big fan of the slider, think it has the chance to be borderline plus\n Changeup has made strides and could be average or a bit better\n Command is fringy, and could lead to more of a swingman type role for him",
    "Notes Updated 3": "7/15/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 3": "2023 Post Draft\nKuehner was one of Louisville’s most important relievers this year. He throws from a tough lefty angle. His fastball was 92–95 this year with a good amount of run. The fastball works up, as well as down in the zone. His breaking ball is a pretty nasty pitch, however he did struggle to command it over the last few seasons. There is potential for Kuehner to be a really solid pen guy. An interesting pickup for what will likely be a well under  slot senior signing.",
